  ],
  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (adding Public School Code Sec. 1322-B(a)): A school entity may, with the approval of the department, enter into a contract or other agreement with a vendor for the lease, purchase, installation, operation or maintenance of a firearm detection technology or other equipment and supplies necessary for the proper operation of the firearm detection technology.\nSec. 1 (adding Public School Code Sec. 1322-B(b)(2)): When a brandished firearm is detected on school property or a school bus, possess the capacity to immediately and independently alert school personnel, first responders or other persons, as determined by the department or school entity, with minimal human oversight.",
